WEBVTT

00:00.950 --> 00:10.790
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:04.990 --> 00:05.810
Whoa!

00:12.520 --> 00:13.800
Squishy, we're here.

00:19.610 --> 00:28.040
Upon Squishy's plea and Shota's recommendation, Satoshi and his friends make a stop here at Terminus Cave on their way to Eisetsu City.

00:30.280 --> 00:32.170
They couldn't possibly have any business in a place like that.

00:32.170 --> 00:33.760
They wouldn't be going in there if they didn't.

00:35.800 --> 00:38.460
Wherever Pikachu goes, the Rocket Gang follows.

00:38.810 --> 00:39.930
After them!

00:39.930 --> 00:40.540
Yeah!

00:40.540 --> 00:41.450
Aw, geez...

00:44.640 --> 00:47.150
This place used to be a mine, but it closed down ages ago.

00:47.550 --> 00:51.660
It's now a habitat for wild Pokémon, which is why Trainers often come by.

00:51.660 --> 00:52.860
Oh, an Ariados!

00:54.270 --> 00:55.400
There's a Tsubotsubo too!

00:57.310 --> 00:57.870
And a Kodora!

00:59.120 --> 01:00.870
It's just as Shota said!

01:05.630 --> 01:06.570
What's the matter?

01:06.570 --> 01:07.550
Eureka!

01:15.210 --> 01:20.880
Terminus Cave!
The Mystery of Z is Set in Motion!!

01:21.950 --> 01:31.820
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

01:21.950 --> 01:31.820
Z

01:22.340 --> 01:23.330
Squishy!

01:23.580 --> 01:25.300
Wait!

01:30.460 --> 01:32.230
Squishy, are you looking for something?

01:34.260 --> 01:36.270
Was that what it wanted to do...?

01:36.660 --> 01:37.220
Oh, right.

01:37.740 --> 01:38.850
Please, Tairenar!

01:42.510 --> 01:44.020
Can you light up this area with your flame?

01:47.810 --> 01:48.530
Thank you!

01:48.850 --> 01:49.940
Now I can see clearly!

01:49.940 --> 01:52.130
In that case, we will assist you!

01:52.660 --> 01:54.050
Citronic Gear, on!

02:16.850 --> 02:19.810
Can you please take a slightly easier route, Squishy...?

02:27.040 --> 02:28.990
We've come pretty far inside.

02:28.990 --> 02:29.620
Yeah.

02:32.580 --> 02:34.140
I wonder how far it will go?

02:35.490 --> 02:35.890
Squishy!

02:48.560 --> 02:49.620
Squishy, wait!

02:49.890 --> 02:51.340
Eureka, watch out!

02:51.870 --> 02:53.580
But Squishy is running off!

02:53.780 --> 02:54.300
Calm down!

02:57.140 --> 02:59.680
Climbing down there is definitely impossible for us...

03:00.130 --> 03:01.500
But we can't leave it on its own!

03:01.810 --> 03:03.090
We need to follow after Squishy!

03:03.550 --> 03:05.120
Don't worry, Eureka.

03:05.520 --> 03:08.030
We'll catch up to it in no time. I have a good idea.

03:09.170 --> 03:10.790
Onbat, I choose you!

03:14.100 --> 03:17.630
Please use your Supersonic to find a route that leads down to the bottom of this cliff.

03:17.940 --> 03:18.580
Please!

03:24.190 --> 03:26.030
Rentorar, we need you too!

03:29.740 --> 03:32.560
Please use your ability to see through objects to find a route as well.

03:32.930 --> 03:33.760
I expected nothing less, Citron!

03:42.750 --> 03:43.820
This way, right?

03:43.820 --> 03:45.580
Thank you, Onbat, Rentorar!

03:47.660 --> 03:49.440
All right, let's go to where Squishy is!

03:49.440 --> 03:49.980
Let's go!

03:58.980 --> 04:00.580
Just how far are they going to go?

04:00.580 --> 04:02.740
They sure are adventurous.

04:02.740 --> 04:04.620
Well, we're going too then...

04:04.860 --> 04:07.250
I wonder what awaits ahead, an exciting adventure, or a treasure maybe?

04:07.250 --> 04:09.950
Wrong! We're here to get Pikachu!

04:38.750 --> 04:39.140
There it is!

04:40.020 --> 04:41.210
Putting up that thing paid off.

04:42.340 --> 04:43.950
Hey, this is <i>Z1!</i>

04:44.290 --> 04:44.710
What?

04:46.320 --> 04:47.210
Headquarters, headquarters!

04:47.920 --> 04:49.970
Z1 has appeared in Terminus Cave!

05:14.080 --> 05:14.490
Rentorar?

05:15.650 --> 05:17.260
You found Squishy, correct?

05:17.260 --> 05:17.730
Let's go!

05:21.890 --> 05:23.570
Are you unharmed?

05:33.660 --> 05:34.590
We are.

05:37.260 --> 05:39.340
We've detected a strong energy wave coming from Z1!

05:39.980 --> 05:41.310
Z2 is responding!

05:42.430 --> 05:44.560
We got Z2's location now!

05:45.020 --> 05:47.380
Momiji, Akebi, go!

05:48.050 --> 05:48.860
Understood!

05:49.230 --> 05:52.110
It may be a legendary entity, but it sure is foolish.

05:52.450 --> 05:54.180
Its location is so obvious.

05:54.180 --> 05:57.570
Our detection system is just too good.

06:01.460 --> 06:04.620
We are in no trouble. Escape!

06:12.480 --> 06:13.250
Squishy!

06:15.410 --> 06:16.310
Thank goodness!

06:18.000 --> 06:20.040
Squishy, you can't run around by yourself any more.

06:20.660 --> 06:21.950
You got us worried!

06:26.740 --> 06:27.390
It vanished?

06:28.300 --> 06:29.420
Squishy, where are you?

06:29.650 --> 06:30.020
Squishy!

06:33.360 --> 06:34.780
I don't get what's happening.

06:35.250 --> 06:36.620
It's one mystery after another.

06:36.620 --> 06:39.030
Just what <i>is</i> Squishy?

06:47.300 --> 06:48.160
We've arrived at the scene.

06:48.510 --> 06:48.850
Understood!

06:48.850 --> 06:50.170
Oh my!

06:50.800 --> 06:52.130
You're late.

06:52.560 --> 06:54.100
There was a lot of traffic!

06:55.940 --> 06:57.570
Was there an accident or something?

06:59.090 --> 07:01.410
Never mind, let's just go. Z1 is waiting.

07:01.780 --> 07:02.670
Right, right.

07:02.940 --> 07:03.890
Follow me.

07:13.280 --> 07:14.610
Squishy, where are you?

07:14.820 --> 07:15.820
Squishy!

07:16.820 --> 07:18.570
Squishy, come out!

07:19.440 --> 07:20.380
How is it, Rentorar?

07:23.760 --> 07:24.510
Onbat, what about you?

07:28.180 --> 07:28.580
Nothing, huh?

07:30.020 --> 07:31.790
Maybe it's not here any more.

07:32.380 --> 07:33.540
That can't be!

07:33.540 --> 07:35.300
It's here! Eureka can tell!

07:39.540 --> 07:40.030
You're right.

07:42.720 --> 07:45.390
Squishy, you're here, right? Please come out!

07:45.580 --> 07:47.900
Please! Squishy, come out!

08:01.740 --> 08:03.760
You kids, don't move!

08:05.730 --> 08:06.850
You guys again!

08:08.180 --> 08:08.800
There they are!

08:09.090 --> 08:10.460
The women with the goggles!

08:19.620 --> 08:20.800
That was a warning shot.

08:21.180 --> 08:22.270
The next one will hit its mark.

08:41.040 --> 08:41.870
Found it!

08:50.130 --> 08:50.410
What's that?

08:50.940 --> 08:51.680
I missed!

08:57.150 --> 08:58.700
Why are those guys shooting into the dark?

08:59.060 --> 09:00.140
No, they can see it.

09:00.350 --> 09:01.380
Squishy, that is.

09:08.240 --> 09:08.960
Something's there!

09:09.170 --> 09:09.850
It's Squishy!

09:24.560 --> 09:25.420
Squishy!

09:28.560 --> 09:29.470
Pokémon Quiz!

09:30.020 --> 09:30.800
The answer is...?

09:41.100 --> 09:41.940
Squishy!

09:41.940 --> 09:42.400
Watch out!

09:46.400 --> 09:47.930
I told you not to move!

09:48.370 --> 09:49.220
Everyone, let's go!

09:49.810 --> 09:50.300
Rentorar!

09:50.300 --> 09:51.500
Tairenar, please!

09:53.220 --> 09:54.020
Delvil!

09:59.520 --> 10:01.170
Onbat, Supersonic!

10:04.240 --> 10:05.090
Tackle!

10:08.050 --> 10:08.830
Dorapion!

10:08.830 --> 10:09.450
You did it!

10:09.860 --> 10:10.830
Iron Head!

10:15.390 --> 10:16.500
Are you all right, Onbat?

10:18.030 --> 10:19.390
Kirikizan, Metal Sound!

10:22.780 --> 10:23.390
Capture it!

10:23.740 --> 10:24.470
Understood!

10:31.420 --> 10:32.380
Ha!

10:34.060 --> 10:34.690
You guys are...!

10:35.840 --> 10:37.700
If you tell us "You guys are...!",

10:38.740 --> 10:40.690
It is the world's mercy that makes us introduce ourselves!

10:41.470 --> 10:43.360
We don't know Squishy's value, but...

10:43.580 --> 10:45.860
...if you guys want it so badly, it must be worth <i>something</i>.

10:46.100 --> 10:48.370
This green guy is ours!

10:48.370 --> 10:50.220
We will not hand it over to you!

10:50.980 --> 10:51.700
Musashi!

10:52.480 --> 10:53.200
Kojiro!

10:53.710 --> 10:56.720
For the Rocket Gang duo dashing across the galaxy,

10:57.260 --> 11:00.420
a white hole, a white tomorrow awaits ahead!

11:00.580 --> 11:02.190
Just kidding!

11:09.790 --> 11:10.180
...And?

11:11.950 --> 11:14.290
That thing you're calling "Z"...

11:14.290 --> 11:16.020
...is now ours!

11:18.380 --> 11:20.000
Where did you get <i>that</i> from?

11:20.320 --> 11:22.620
I dislike people like you.

11:24.540 --> 11:26.220
Go, Gekkouga!

11:28.860 --> 11:30.210
We'll help Squishy!

11:36.510 --> 11:38.180
That's ours!

11:38.880 --> 11:39.950
Cross Poison!

11:44.770 --> 11:45.970
Stone Edge!

11:51.870 --> 11:52.850
Back it up, Pikachu!

11:53.260 --> 11:54.100
Thunderbolt!

11:56.690 --> 11:57.710
Flamethrower!

11:59.550 --> 12:00.720
Swift!

12:04.380 --> 12:05.710
Dark Pulse!

12:22.690 --> 12:23.940
Thank you, Gekkouga.

12:23.940 --> 12:24.710
Good job.

12:25.500 --> 12:27.170
Squishy, are you all right?

12:30.960 --> 12:34.430
That's no mere "Squishy" you're talking to.

12:34.740 --> 12:36.260
For us, the Flare Gang, it's an important...

12:36.740 --> 12:37.970
Correa, that's enough.

12:38.570 --> 12:40.300
Why don't you tell us?

12:40.300 --> 12:42.690
If it's no "mere" Squishy, what kind of Squishy is it?

12:43.300 --> 12:46.430
We're not nice enough to educate idiots.

12:46.690 --> 12:48.350
Dorapion, Sludge Bomb!

12:59.170 --> 13:00.530
Hand over that little one, will you?

13:03.900 --> 13:05.010
I'll protect you, no matter what.

13:05.810 --> 13:07.470
I promised that I won't let you go.

13:09.630 --> 13:10.980
There's nothing to be done about this child...

13:11.260 --> 13:11.660
Get them.

13:16.660 --> 13:17.390
Don't tell me...!

13:18.400 --> 13:18.910
What's this?

13:28.290 --> 13:28.660
Cell...

13:29.150 --> 13:29.730
So many?

13:30.670 --> 13:31.170
"Cell"?

13:31.650 --> 13:32.740
Are they Squishy's friends?

13:59.140 --> 13:59.840
Squishy?

14:00.320 --> 14:01.270
They merged?

14:01.580 --> 14:04.380
Is this an evolution?

14:05.090 --> 14:06.500
So this is what you saw.

14:06.800 --> 14:07.280
Yes.

14:26.190 --> 14:27.960
I had no idea Squishy had that kind of power!

14:52.290 --> 14:53.010
Squishy!

15:00.880 --> 15:02.480
Follow it, Lepardas!

15:05.170 --> 15:06.370
Livolt, follow it!

15:09.170 --> 15:11.540
Pikachu, Gekkouga, stop those guys!

15:23.840 --> 15:25.520
Lepardas, Shadow Claw!

15:29.760 --> 15:30.890
Cut!

15:39.120 --> 15:40.120
Thunderbolt!

15:47.730 --> 15:48.510
Iron Tail!

15:56.210 --> 15:57.590
Are you all right, Gekkouga?

15:58.460 --> 16:00.140
It's over for Gekkouga, don't you think?

16:00.670 --> 16:01.460
Satoshi!

16:04.160 --> 16:05.380
Geez, how unpleasant.

16:06.240 --> 16:08.600
You're in the way. Hurry up and back off!

16:09.060 --> 16:10.800
Gekkouga, can you keep going?

16:14.940 --> 16:15.610
All right.

16:15.980 --> 16:17.990
Let's go!

16:26.620 --> 16:27.870
Water Shuriken!

16:29.660 --> 16:30.590
Shock Wave!

16:35.500 --> 16:36.190
Scratch!

16:43.050 --> 16:43.540
What is this?

16:48.380 --> 16:49.520
Cut!

16:55.940 --> 16:56.780
Shadow Claw!

16:57.710 --> 16:58.930
Aerial Ace!

17:16.210 --> 17:17.330
It's pointless to keep this up.

17:17.620 --> 17:18.430
Agreed.

17:18.900 --> 17:20.130
Livolt, Flash!

17:23.740 --> 17:25.700
Let's revise our plan as well!

17:26.610 --> 17:27.340
Roger!

17:48.820 --> 17:50.340
Satoshi, are you all right?

17:50.540 --> 17:51.010
Yeah.

17:51.420 --> 17:52.510
What happened?

17:52.930 --> 17:54.770
It was the same thing that happened in the Ninja Village.

17:55.390 --> 17:55.980
Yeah.

17:55.980 --> 17:58.610
It somehow felt like I became Gekkouga.

17:58.910 --> 17:59.590
"Became"?

17:59.790 --> 18:00.170
Yep.

18:00.620 --> 18:02.670
Hey, which way did Squishy go?

18:04.270 --> 18:06.500
We still haven't discovered Z1.

18:06.930 --> 18:09.070
Understood. Keep standing by there.

18:09.730 --> 18:11.650
Oh my, it got away.

18:12.670 --> 18:14.460
There's a possibility that it's still nearby.

18:16.270 --> 18:16.650
What?

18:17.710 --> 18:20.940
Since those Trainers seem to have a connection to Z1,

18:21.280 --> 18:22.480
it's worth marking them.

18:22.900 --> 18:23.900
I see.

18:23.900 --> 18:24.430
Hey!

18:25.780 --> 18:28.170
What? You guys again?

18:28.560 --> 18:31.410
That brat boy is <i>our</i> prey.

18:31.760 --> 18:33.900
We won't allow you to interfere!

18:34.180 --> 18:34.660
Also!

18:35.250 --> 18:37.180
I don't know what you're plotting,

18:37.650 --> 18:39.330
but let me tell you this:

18:39.330 --> 18:41.420
The world belongs to our Sakaki-sama!

18:41.870 --> 18:43.630
It belongs to the Rocket Gang!

18:46.780 --> 18:47.440
Ha!

18:50.080 --> 18:50.720
So lame...

18:51.390 --> 18:52.130
And so annoying...

18:53.310 --> 18:54.880
Squishy!

18:55.090 --> 18:56.900
Hey, Squishy!

18:56.900 --> 18:59.020
Come out, please!

18:58.220 --> 18:59.370
Squishy!

19:01.250 --> 19:02.130
It's not here.

19:02.560 --> 19:05.820
If it ran from those guys, it might be hiding somewhere.

19:06.350 --> 19:09.380
Either that, or it did not want to cause us trouble...

19:09.790 --> 19:10.770
No!

19:13.100 --> 19:16.130
It protected us, remember?

19:16.880 --> 19:18.480
Squishy is our friend.

19:18.850 --> 19:21.130
It must be waiting for us somewhere!

19:22.450 --> 19:23.120
You're right.

19:24.290 --> 19:25.840
It is exactly as you say, Eureka.

19:31.490 --> 19:31.890
Yeah.

19:33.460 --> 19:34.800
Wait for us, Squishy!

19:35.840 --> 19:39.280
More and more mysteries appear before Satoshi and his friends.

19:36.910 --> 19:46.780
The next episode will air Thursday January 14th, 2016 at 7pm! Look forward to it!!

19:39.950 --> 19:41.810
Squishy has left Eureka's side.

19:42.380 --> 19:45.950
But just what <i>is</i> Squishy?

19:46.430 --> 19:47.470
To be continued...

19:50.900 --> 19:52.990
We finally got a clear image of it.

19:53.300 --> 19:55.870
This is the form Z1 takes when it merges with Cell.

19:56.350 --> 19:58.590
You could call it a more dynamic form.

19:58.860 --> 20:01.060
This one's worth researching.

20:01.490 --> 20:04.400
I'm sure that's not all there is to Z's power.

20:05.250 --> 20:06.450
By the way, what about Z2?

20:07.170 --> 20:11.390
We're tracking it at present. Its capture is a matter of time.

20:15.880 --> 20:20.850
Sunday December 27th
at 8am!

20:15.880 --> 20:18.410
Outburst of Pokémon phantasies!?

20:15.880 --> 20:18.410
Yudai Chiba

20:16.350 --> 20:18.410
I took my Monozu to the hairdresser and told him, "Cut it like this".

20:16.530 --> 20:19.820
Actor Yudai Chiba-kun's visit at Pokénchi causes great excitement!

20:21.300 --> 20:22.180
Ta-da!

20:22.400 --> 20:24.670
The Super-Exquisite Christmas Present Quiz!

20:24.990 --> 20:26.240
These are the presents!

20:26.980 --> 20:28.850
First, a Satoshi Gekkouga Moncollé!

20:29.120 --> 20:31.330
It played a big role in today's episode, right?

20:32.300 --> 20:37.390
Also, Pokémon Tretta with Satoshi Gekkouga, Xerneas, Yveltal and Zygarde!

20:38.350 --> 20:42.240
Finally, a Satoshi Gekkouga EX anime collab card!

20:43.170 --> 20:49.120
The Moncollé figure, the Tretta and the card will be given away as a set to 100 people via lottery.

20:50.130 --> 20:51.120
Okay, here's the question:

20:51.630 --> 20:55.940
In today's episode, which of the following was the Flare Gang after?

20:56.960 --> 20:58.080
A: Pikachu,

21:00.160 --> 21:01.360
B: Gekkouga...

21:04.050 --> 21:05.250
...or C: Squishy?

21:06.320 --> 21:09.600
All right! Call the number you think is correct!

21:10.210 --> 21:14.820
Answer the quiz and get a super-exquisite Christmas present!

